Four patches against pristine crossover-sources-26.3.0.tar.gz, published by
CodeWeavers. They are modifications to Wine and are LGPL-2.1-or-later; the full
text is in ../fixes/LICENSE.LGPL, and ../NOTICE.md says what belongs to whom.

THESE FOUR ARE THE ONES FIFA 17 NEEDS, AND THE ONLY ONES build.sh APPLIES

If this folder holds any other patch, it is unrelated FIFA 15 work kept in the
development tree: not in build.sh's PATCHES list, not used to build anything in
fixes/, and not tested against FIFA 17. Ignore it.

APPLY ORDER MATTERS, AND IT IS NOT ALPHABETICAL

    1. crossover-26.3-fifa17-rosetta.patch
    2. crossover-26.3-fifa17-online.patch
    3. crossover-26.3-fifa17-audio.patch
    4. crossover-26.3-fifa17-cng.patch

cng must go last: it builds on online, and both touch dlls/crypt32/pfx.c.
Applying them in directory order -- the obvious thing to do with a folder of
patches -- produces a reject.

    patch -p1 --forward < ../patches/<name>          # from the wine/ directory

WHAT EACH ONE COVERS

    rosetta   bugs 1-8    getting the game to boot and run at all
                          ntdll (signal_x86_64.c, virtual.c, loader), version
    online    bugs 9-12   getting online to work
                          ntdll/unix/virtual.c, crypt32/pfx.c, secur32/schannel.c
    audio     bug 4       getting sound back, plus two Wine bugs beside it
                          winecoreaudio.drv
    cng       bug 13      CNG and PKCS#12, so .NET can use a certificate
                          crypt32 (both halves), include/wincrypt.h

Each patch carries its own header explaining what it changes and why, including
the reasoning and the measurements behind it. Read the top of the file before
the diff.

ONE THING A PATCH CANNOT CARRY

SONAME_LIBGNUTLS is undefined in this tree, which is a configure result and not
source. Without defining it, the whole unix half of crypt32 compiles to stubs
that return STATUS_DLL_NOT_FOUND -- the PE side reports "call not implemented"
-- and it does that while building perfectly cleanly. In your build64 directory:

    sed -i '' 's|/\* #undef SONAME_LIBGNUTLS \*/|#define SONAME_LIBGNUTLS "libgnutls.30.dylib"|' \
        include/config.h
    ln -s "$(brew --prefix gnutls)/include/gnutls" include/gnutls

Only the headers are needed; CrossOver 26.3 already ships libgnutls.30.dylib in
its lib64 directory and crypt32 opens it by name at runtime.

../build.sh does all of the above for you, including this step.
